1
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,060
I see.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:06,040
So you're an adventurer.

3
00:00:07,610 --> 00:00:11,670
I wanted to be one a long time ago.

4
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:18,000
It was the kind of dumb
childhood dream everyone has.

5
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:25,060
<i>Like a fairy tale</i>

6
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:27,480
<i>It's a sign the story has reached its end</i>

7
00:00:27,480 --> 00:00:30,400
<i>Like a single passage taken from</i>

8
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,030
<i>A journey that was too long</i>

9
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:34,360
<i>Of the evil that once cast a shadow</i>

10
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:36,700
<i>Across this land</i>

11
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,030
<i>And the memories of the short journey</i>

12
00:00:39,030 --> 00:00:41,490
<i>With the hero who defeated it</i>

13
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:53,800
<i>The story ends</i>

14
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,300
<i>And the hero goes to sleep</i>

15
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:59,140
<i>Leaving this land with</i>

16
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:00,810
<i>Days of peace and quiet</i>

17
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:03,310
<i>The passage of time heartlessly</i>

18
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:05,480
<i>Makes people forget</i>

19
00:01:05,480 --> 00:01:08,270
<i>Even the tracks left behind by his life</i>

20
00:01:08,270 --> 00:01:10,060
<i>Begin to rust</i>

21
00:01:10,060 --> 00:01:11,900
<i>Just the same</i>

22
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,190
<i>Your words and wishes and courage</i>

23
00:01:14,190 --> 00:01:17,530
<i>Are still inside of me</i>

24
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:19,410
<i>And they live on</i>

25
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:21,950
<i>We chose the same path</i>

26
00:01:21,950 --> 00:01:24,080
<i>That's all it was supposed to be</i>

27
00:01:24,080 --> 00:01:25,620
<i>Why is it that at some point</i>

28
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:29,880
<i>I wanted to understand the reason for</i>

29
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,250
<i>The tears that fall down my cheeks</i>

30
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:32,340
<i>Even now</i>

31
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:34,710
<i>If I retrace the journey we walked together</i>

32
00:01:34,710 --> 00:01:38,260
<i>Even though you're not there</i>

33
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:39,930
<i>I know I'll be able to find it</i>

34
00:01:58,370 --> 00:02:00,030
When I was a kid,

35
00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:04,770
I had a friend who I joined
on lots of little adventures.

36
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:10,030
Foolhardy and with energy to spare,
he was like a gorilla.

37
00:02:10,950 --> 00:02:14,640
That said, he was a good gorilla
who cared for his friends.

38
00:02:16,230 --> 00:02:20,060
When I grew up and started
to forget that dream,

39
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:25,660
he invited me to become
an adventurer with him.

40
00:02:27,260 --> 00:02:32,270
I wonder what would've changed
if I'd taken his hand then.

41
00:02:33,870 --> 00:02:36,020
That was ten years ago.

42
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:38,580
I still regret it.

43
00:02:39,710 --> 00:02:40,990
Huh.

44
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:44,070
So why are you telling me this?

45
00:02:44,760 --> 00:02:48,060
My village's harvest festival is coming up.

46
00:02:48,060 --> 00:02:53,110
My brother asked me to go into the woods
and pick wild herbs to use in cooking.

47
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:54,070
But then...

48
00:02:56,320 --> 00:02:58,460
I got stuck in a bottomless swamp.

49
00:02:59,070 --> 00:03:02,590
I'm done for.

50
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:09,810
But if you take my hand,
then maybe my fate will change.

51
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:13,890
Hold on. I'm thinking about it.

52
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:18,870
What is there to think about?

53
00:03:18,870 --> 00:03:20,110
Your hand is dirty.

54
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:23,890
This is really not the time
to be worrying about that!

55
00:03:25,220 --> 00:03:26,660
Besides, miss...

56
00:03:27,870 --> 00:03:31,480
Grown-ups are dirty by nature.

57
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:36,300
This might be my first time encountering
a physically dirty adult.

58
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:38,580
Can I have some more time?

59
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:42,500
I'm trying to remember the spell to pull
someone out of a bottomless swamp.

60
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:45,540
P-Please hurry.

61
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:46,980
Let's see...

62
00:03:47,490 --> 00:03:48,770
Ms. Frieren.

63
00:03:49,090 --> 00:03:51,120
Did you find any herbs?

64
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:52,980
Oh, I remember now.

65
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:01,080
This is far enough.

66
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:04,310
I'm sorry for the trouble
Ms. Frieren caused you.

67
00:04:04,310 --> 00:04:08,180
It's fine. She saved me.

68
00:04:08,180 --> 00:04:11,780
I'll give her an earful later.

69
00:04:12,230 --> 00:04:13,410
Not my problem.

70
00:04:14,050 --> 00:04:17,500
Anyway, are you sure you don't
need to stop by the village?

71
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:21,170
We're busy preparing for the harvest festival,
but I can at least thank you.

72
00:04:21,570 --> 00:04:26,840
We're hoping to reach a large
town today so we can resupply.

73
00:04:27,070 --> 00:04:30,170
I see. In that case, be careful.

74
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:33,270
There are lots of dangerous
venomous creatures around here.

75
00:04:33,630 --> 00:04:34,370
Okay.

76
00:04:34,370 --> 00:04:35,520
Got it.

77
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:46,780
Something bit me.

78
00:04:47,320 --> 00:04:49,650
What? You were bitten?

79
00:04:49,650 --> 00:04:53,450
He told us to be careful.
What are you doing?

80
00:04:53,450 --> 00:04:55,380
Let's stop the bleeding.

81
00:04:55,860 --> 00:04:56,610
Huh?

82
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:59,250
My nose is starting to bleed.

83
00:05:01,720 --> 00:05:06,710
Identifying poison is a priest spell,
so I'm not too good at it.

84
00:05:06,710 --> 00:05:10,810
I don't recognize this reaction,
so the antidotes we have might not work.

85
00:05:11,170 --> 00:05:13,610
We should get you checked out at a church.

86
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:17,660
Fern, how much longer can
you use your flying magic?

87
00:05:17,660 --> 00:05:21,950
It consumes a lot of mana,
so only about thirty minutes.

88
00:05:21,950 --> 00:05:25,100
Thirty minutes won't get us to town.

89
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:27,170
We'll head back to that village.

90
00:05:27,170 --> 00:05:29,390
I'll transport Stark.

91
00:05:29,390 --> 00:05:30,980
It's not that big a deal.

92
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:33,170
I'm fine.

93
00:05:33,170 --> 00:05:36,620
Besides, my master said
you can tough out poisons.

94
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:41,720
Come to think of it, Eisen was perfectly
healthy even after taking several arrows

95
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:45,240
that were coated with a poison
strong enough to knock out a dragon.

96
00:05:45,930 --> 00:05:48,140
Heiter was appalled.

97
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:49,420
See?

98
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:54,440
That just goes to show that Mr. Eisen
was far from normal.

99
00:05:54,440 --> 00:06:01,150
Besides, according to Mr. Heiter,
20% of adventurer deaths are due to poison.

100
00:06:02,090 --> 00:06:03,260
We should hurry.

101
00:06:04,960 --> 00:06:08,140
I'm fine, really.

102
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,270
It's too late.

103
00:06:15,610 --> 00:06:18,340
In a few hours, his brain
will begin to melt.

104
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:20,530
It will flow out his nose,

105
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:22,510
and then he'll die.

106
00:06:22,510 --> 00:06:24,210
That's terrifying!

107
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:27,620
Isn't there anything we can do, Father?

108
00:06:27,890 --> 00:06:32,360
Normally, it can only be
cured if it's treated early,

109
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:34,760
but perhaps my brother could help.

110
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:38,020
Brother, do you have a minute?

111
00:06:38,250 --> 00:06:40,810
Don't you think this new
tub is kind of small?

112
00:06:40,810 --> 00:06:42,350
There's honor in poverty.

113
00:06:42,350 --> 00:06:43,990
Isn't this going too far, though?

114
00:06:44,450 --> 00:06:48,270
We're the only ones who impoverish
ourselves down to a hand-sized tub.

115
00:06:48,670 --> 00:06:52,660
More importantly, Sein,
take a look at this boy.

116
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:56,540
Huh? Brother, these are the
ones I told you about.

117
00:06:56,970 --> 00:06:59,030
They're the people who rescued me.

118
00:07:00,650 --> 00:07:04,130
Did you get bitten by a snake?

119
00:07:04,130 --> 00:07:06,040
I told you to be careful.

120
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:14,570
Now we're even.

121
00:07:14,950 --> 00:07:17,690
Brother, I'm going to help out at the plaza.

122
00:07:18,530 --> 00:07:19,480
Sure.

123
00:07:21,290 --> 00:07:24,240
My nose stopped bleeding.

124
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:27,580
The effects of the poison are gone.

125
00:07:30,540 --> 00:07:32,620
Father, is he...?

126
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:36,940
What do you think of my younger brother?

127
00:07:39,510 --> 00:07:42,440
That holy symbol around your neck

128
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:46,710
is awarded to the most outstanding priest
in a region by the holy capital.

129
00:07:47,770 --> 00:07:52,960
He instantly cured a poison a
healing expert called incurable.

130
00:07:54,040 --> 00:07:56,040
He's a genius.

131
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:59,830
I'm not surprised you noticed, Ms. Frieren.

132
00:07:59,830 --> 00:08:02,140
You know who I am?

133
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:05,100
Mr. Heiter told me about you.

134
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:13,050
He gave me this holy symbol when he came
here from the holy capital to observe us.

135
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:17,190
That said, I'm a mere provincial priest.

136
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:21,200
This is the only thing I can be proud of.

137
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:25,870
But my ability doesn't compare to Sein's.

138
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:30,440
Our parents passed away when we were young.

139
00:08:31,150 --> 00:08:35,460
Since then, I raised my much
younger brother myself.

140
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:41,290
As a child, he often said he wanted
to become an adventurer.

141
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:43,870
He didn't want to become

142
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:49,580
an ordinary village priest like me
who spent every day the same way.

143
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:53,850
He said that with his eyes
full of hopes and dreams.

144
00:08:54,790 --> 00:08:59,170
But now he's like I was when I was young.

145
00:08:59,870 --> 00:09:02,320
This life must bore him.

146
00:09:03,890 --> 00:09:08,640
Would you please take him
away from this village?

147
00:09:09,070 --> 00:09:14,710
I'm certain he's been looking for someone
to give him that last push.

148
00:09:18,050 --> 00:09:20,360
I'm in, Frieren.

149
00:09:20,930 --> 00:09:23,190
What's there to even think about?

150
00:09:24,720 --> 00:09:28,480
I'm not risking my brains
flowing out my nose again.

151
00:09:28,940 --> 00:09:33,560
It's true that the journey ahead
may be safer with a priest.

152
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:36,740
What do you not like about
the idea, Ms. Frieren?

153
00:09:38,810 --> 00:09:41,860
It's an aversion to my own kind, I guess.

154
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:44,210
What is she talking about?

155
00:09:44,710 --> 00:09:48,580
I'm inviting him to join us,
even if you two don't want to.

156
00:09:51,390 --> 00:09:52,530
Where is he going?

157
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:57,250
Mr. Sein spends a lot of time
at the bar downstairs.

158
00:09:57,740 --> 00:09:58,790
What?

159
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:02,510
Alcohol.

160
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:04,890
Tobacco.

161
00:10:06,070 --> 00:10:07,020
Gambling.

162
00:10:09,450 --> 00:10:11,970
That's a bit <i>too</i> corrupt, don't you think?

163
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:16,130
I'm getting to know the people.
Care to join us?

164
00:10:16,840 --> 00:10:20,980
It's Stark. We're looking for a priest.

165
00:10:21,470 --> 00:10:22,870
Will you join us?

166
00:10:24,360 --> 00:10:28,600
You must be joking.
I'm this village's priest.

167
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:30,140
I can't go on adventures.

168
00:10:32,260 --> 00:10:35,470
No, I suppose that could be fun.

169
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:37,920
Have a seat, Stark.

170
00:10:38,310 --> 00:10:40,820
If you can beat me, I'll join your party.

171
00:10:40,820 --> 00:10:42,000
Really?

172
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,920
Yes, really.

173
00:10:46,660 --> 00:10:49,740
Please, no!

174
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:54,690
Ms. Frieren, I think I heard
Mr. Stark scream downstairs.

175
00:11:04,170 --> 00:11:06,200
Someone's taken all his belongings.

176
00:11:06,890 --> 00:11:09,550
How awful. Who would do this?

177
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:11,140
No hard feelings.

178
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:11,830
What?

179
00:11:12,870 --> 00:11:16,440
Grown-ups are dirty, after all.

180
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:18,990
Someone's taken all <i>his</i> belongings!

181
00:11:18,990 --> 00:11:21,260
The village chief won the lot.

182
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:23,430
He's got the devil's own luck.

183
00:11:23,870 --> 00:11:24,690
Sein.

184
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:28,940
I heard you're looking for party members.
Ask someone else.

185
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:31,820
You want to become an adventurer, don't you?

186
00:11:32,130 --> 00:11:36,400
That was a long time ago. It's too late now.

187
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:40,470
I should've gone after him sooner.

188
00:11:41,890 --> 00:11:45,210
The only person sitting here
is a loser in his underwear.

189
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:52,670
Frieren, come defeat the Demon King with us.

190
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,220
It's too late now.

191
00:11:54,650 --> 00:11:58,300
I haven't fought demons in over 500 years.

192
00:11:58,850 --> 00:12:01,590
I've forgotten how to fight them.

193
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:05,730
I deferred the decision for too long.

194
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:09,610
I was probably afraid to fight the Demon King.

195
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:13,910
Too much time has passed.
Time I can't get back now.

196
00:12:14,990 --> 00:12:17,120
So what, Frieren?

197
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:20,550
I'm talking about the present.

198
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:31,280
Ask someone else.

199
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,300
You don't know how I feel.

200
00:12:34,810 --> 00:12:38,070
I see. That told me everything I need to know.

201
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:40,710
I don't like you, Sein.

202
00:12:42,630 --> 00:12:44,990
I see. In that case...

203
00:12:44,990 --> 00:12:47,840
So I've decided you'll join us,
no matter what.

204
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:51,000
What? Why?

205
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:54,930
That makes so little sense that it scares me.

206
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:58,700
Thanks. I feel warmer now.

207
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:05,310
I'm truly sorry for all the
trouble we caused. Excuse us.

208
00:13:07,430 --> 00:13:09,330
How much did it cost to get everything back?

209
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:12,920
He said we should take our time and
enjoy the harvest festival coming up,

210
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:15,530
and then he returned it all for free.

211
00:13:15,530 --> 00:13:18,150
Good thing they're nice people here.

212
00:13:18,150 --> 00:13:20,510
He didn't know what to do with the axe.

213
00:13:20,510 --> 00:13:21,670
That's kinda sad.

214
00:13:22,650 --> 00:13:24,660
Mr. Stark, please put these on.

215
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:28,830
Do you have to hold them
like they're filthy?

216
00:13:29,400 --> 00:13:31,340
Mr. Sein, these are yours.

217
00:13:35,370 --> 00:13:38,390
What did I do to upset her?

218
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,740
She's mad you took all
of Stark's belongings.

219
00:13:43,170 --> 00:13:46,010
It wasn't me. It was the chief.

220
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:50,030
People who gamble are the worst.

221
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:52,030
I'm sorry, okay?

222
00:13:52,030 --> 00:13:54,770
And Mr. Sein is supposed to be a priest.

223
00:13:55,190 --> 00:13:57,430
I'm not so sure about a priest who drinks.

224
00:13:58,020 --> 00:14:00,980
Don't you know, Ms. Frieren?

225
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:03,260
Alcohol is the best medicine.

226
00:14:03,260 --> 00:14:06,670
What did you teach her, Heiter?

227
00:14:07,410 --> 00:14:13,780
Whether we recruit him or not,
Sein should become an adventurer.

228
00:14:13,780 --> 00:14:16,690
You've really come around to the idea.

229
00:14:17,810 --> 00:14:21,520
I thought it might be nice to give
someone the push they need,

230
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:24,390
like Himmel the Hero did for me.

231
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:35,150
<i>Looks like the adventurers
have decided to stay in town.</i>

232
00:14:40,100 --> 00:14:43,590
<i>They've been trying
to recruit me every day since.</i>

233
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:51,610
<i>All my efforts to make them stop
have been in vain.</i>

234
00:14:52,550 --> 00:14:59,370
<i>They invite me on adventures with hopes and
dreams in their eyes, like he did back then.</i>

235
00:15:00,410 --> 00:15:03,670
<i>I'm just going to travel around
the northern lands a bit.</i>

236
00:15:04,710 --> 00:15:07,480
I'll be back in time for the harvest
festival three years from now.

237
00:15:07,880 --> 00:15:11,240
If you aren't ready now, you can come then.

238
00:15:12,350 --> 00:15:14,590
<i>Let's go on our next adventure together.</i>

239
00:15:16,210 --> 00:15:21,260
<i>Every time they try to recruit me,
I wonder, "Why now?"</i>

240
00:15:22,180 --> 00:15:25,880
<i>They shine too brightly for these tired eyes.</i>

241
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:30,510
You want to know what Sein likes?

242
00:15:30,510 --> 00:15:34,470
We've been struggling to win him over,
so we're looking for ideas.

243
00:15:34,470 --> 00:15:39,030
Well, he likes alcohol,
tobacco, and gambling...

244
00:15:39,030 --> 00:15:40,910
We know those already.

245
00:15:40,910 --> 00:15:42,910
Are you sure he's a priest?

246
00:15:42,910 --> 00:15:46,860
It seems Mr. Heiter was a
serious priest after all.

247
00:15:47,870 --> 00:15:50,250
What's a serious priest, anyway?

248
00:15:50,530 --> 00:15:55,040
He also likes older women.

249
00:15:55,300 --> 00:15:57,260
He's a totally depraved priest.

250
00:15:57,260 --> 00:15:59,630
Older women, huh?

251
00:16:00,070 --> 00:16:03,070
Honestly, I don't know what
to do with that information.

252
00:16:05,090 --> 00:16:07,180
What?

253
00:16:08,770 --> 00:16:10,230
Oh, right.

254
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:14,410
Brother, don't you think
our new sickle is too small?

255
00:16:14,410 --> 00:16:16,190
You can't even cut grass with...

256
00:16:16,190 --> 00:16:18,750
Oh, it's you again.

257
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,630
Do you have a minute, Sein?

258
00:16:22,630 --> 00:16:23,990
You're still here?

259
00:16:23,990 --> 00:16:24,980
C'mon.

260
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:29,260
Don't make me say it again.
Ask someone else.

261
00:16:30,570 --> 00:16:34,950
Sein, wouldn't you like to
travel with an older woman?

262
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:37,060
Are you stupid?

263
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:42,120
That's the whole reason I wanted
to become an adventurer as a kid.

264
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,330
Talk about impure motives.

265
00:16:43,590 --> 00:16:48,090
So, where is this older woman?

266
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:50,180
Right here, Sein.

267
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:55,640
I'm an elf. I'm far older than you are.

268
00:16:57,450 --> 00:17:00,740
Come to think of it, I think
my brother mentioned that.

269
00:17:05,130 --> 00:17:09,050
But an older woman like that...
is no older woman at all!

270
00:17:09,050 --> 00:17:10,740
He seems really distressed.

271
00:17:10,990 --> 00:17:12,410
Then you leave me with no choice.

272
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:16,350
I didn't want to do this...

273
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:22,580
but the time has come to use the seduction
technique my master taught me.

274
00:17:24,610 --> 00:17:25,370
Smooch.

275
00:17:30,850 --> 00:17:31,990
What was that?

276
00:17:33,450 --> 00:17:35,320
I threw you a kiss.

277
00:17:35,320 --> 00:17:37,670
Maybe you're too young
to appreciate it, sonny.

278
00:17:38,190 --> 00:17:41,340
Won't somebody please take this child home?

279
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:43,090
That was way too sexy.

280
00:17:43,090 --> 00:17:44,780
What's wrong with you two?

281
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:50,620
That's odd. When I tried it on Himmel,
it knocked him out cold.

282
00:17:53,640 --> 00:17:55,230
Himmel!

283
00:17:55,230 --> 00:17:57,110
You're a wicked woman.

284
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,750
How strange.

285
00:17:58,750 --> 00:18:00,070
I understand.

286
00:18:00,070 --> 00:18:03,460
If I'd been the target,
I would have been in danger.

287
00:18:03,460 --> 00:18:05,890
As depraved as he is, he's still a holy man.

288
00:18:05,890 --> 00:18:07,270
A formidable foe.

289
00:18:07,270 --> 00:18:08,810
Enough already.

290
00:18:09,550 --> 00:18:12,240
I'm not becoming an adventurer.

291
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:15,370
I thought you wanted to go after your friend.

292
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:18,620
Brother, you must understand.

293
00:18:19,830 --> 00:18:20,800
Sein...

294
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,830
He said he'd be back in three years.

295
00:18:25,580 --> 00:18:27,540
Well, it's been ten.

296
00:18:28,340 --> 00:18:31,310
He's obviously dead.

297
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:37,110
So you're giving up without going to see him?

298
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,170
It's only been ten years.

299
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:45,280
If you don't go see him now,
you'll regret it in the near future.

300
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:49,370
You'll wonder if you could've made it
in time if you'd gone now.

301
00:18:50,570 --> 00:18:52,000
It's too—

302
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,780
You think it's too late, don't you?

303
00:18:55,940 --> 00:19:00,040
I'm talking about the present, Sein.

304
00:19:05,330 --> 00:19:11,290
I can't go for the same reason
I didn't follow him ten years ago.

305
00:19:11,990 --> 00:19:17,080
I can't leave my brother
behind in this village.

306
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:20,210
What are you talking about, Sein?

307
00:19:21,630 --> 00:19:24,540
I overheard the conversation
you had with Mr. Heiter

308
00:19:24,540 --> 00:19:26,030
when he came to observe us.

309
00:19:27,930 --> 00:19:33,380
With your talent, you could serve
as a priest in the holy capital.

310
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:35,420
Me, in the holy capital?

311
00:19:35,830 --> 00:19:38,230
Yes, undoubtedly.

312
00:19:38,230 --> 00:19:42,680
What would happen to my brother then?

313
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:44,990
He'd come with you, of course.

314
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:47,420
I see.

315
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:52,100
Mr. Heiter, I appreciate the offer,

316
00:19:52,830 --> 00:19:56,670
but my life in this village is comfortable.

317
00:19:57,160 --> 00:20:00,430
My brother lost his parents
when he was still young.

318
00:20:01,170 --> 00:20:03,200
As his older brother,

319
00:20:03,890 --> 00:20:07,510
I can't take his hometown from him, too.

320
00:20:11,190 --> 00:20:12,450
Very well.

321
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:16,600
I understand.

322
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:19,510
I suppose I wasted my time coming here.

323
00:20:19,510 --> 00:20:21,840
But since I'm already wasting time,

324
00:20:22,190 --> 00:20:27,760
perhaps I'll tell your brother
all about my adventures.

325
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:32,170
My brother stayed in this village for me.

326
00:20:34,310 --> 00:20:37,740
Sein, is that what you thought?

327
00:20:41,130 --> 00:20:43,360
We're not the same!

328
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:47,610
I've never regretted the choice I made!

329
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:50,570
But what about you?

330
00:20:50,570 --> 00:20:53,060
How long do you intend
to regret <i>your</i> choice?

331
00:20:53,550 --> 00:20:54,560
I've had enough.

332
00:21:10,990 --> 00:21:13,010
I apologized to my brother.

333
00:21:13,530 --> 00:21:14,370
Okay.

334
00:21:15,260 --> 00:21:19,800
Don't get the wrong idea.
He's a kind brother.

335
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:22,700
He never once hit me before,

336
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:26,440
but I made him hit me this time.

337
00:21:27,020 --> 00:21:29,660
I'd never seen him with
that expression before.

338
00:21:34,200 --> 00:21:38,430
Frieren, I've decided to
become an adventurer.

339
00:21:38,990 --> 00:21:40,440
I'm going after my friend.

340
00:21:41,750 --> 00:21:44,070
It's only been ten years, after all.

341
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:45,700
I see.

342
00:21:51,430 --> 00:21:55,300
I'm doing this so I can look for him.

343
00:21:55,970 --> 00:22:00,970
I'll find him and make my stupid
childhood dream come true.

344
00:22:01,540 --> 00:22:05,780
So I'm only traveling with you partway.

345
00:22:07,120 --> 00:22:08,310
All right!

346
00:22:08,310 --> 00:22:09,400
You did it.

347
00:22:15,420 --> 00:22:16,530
Bye!

348
00:22:16,530 --> 00:22:17,490
See you!

349
00:22:17,490 --> 00:22:18,410
Bye-bye!

350
00:22:18,410 --> 00:22:19,750
See you later!

351
00:22:19,750 --> 00:22:21,420
Later!

352
00:22:25,110 --> 00:22:28,910
By the way, where are you guys headed?

353
00:22:28,910 --> 00:22:30,150
Heaven.

354
00:22:30,500 --> 00:22:32,920
Is that someplace you need to seek out?

355
00:22:33,230 --> 00:22:35,170
We all go there when we die.

356
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,560
Even you, Mr. Sein?

357
00:22:38,460 --> 00:22:42,130
She really doesn't mince words, huh?

358
00:22:42,130 --> 00:22:43,830
Good luck to us both.

359
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:48,180
Seriously, what's her deal?

360
00:22:50,070 --> 00:22:52,620
<i>And you alright</i>

361
00:22:53,120 --> 00:22:55,120
<i>Can you hear me</i>

362
00:22:55,910 --> 00:23:02,000
<i>Trailing along deserted train tracks</i>

363
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,340
<i>Crying excessively</i>

364
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:07,510
<i>Wanting you to smile</i>

365
00:23:07,510 --> 00:23:13,550
<i>I hold on to memories I'd like to keep fresh</i>

366
00:23:13,550 --> 00:23:17,270
<i>There's something I'd like to tell you</i>

367
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:20,020
<i>With words more precious than a goodbye</i>

368
00:23:20,020 --> 00:23:25,690
<i>Unremarkable yet special</i>

369
00:23:25,690 --> 00:23:29,240
<i>See, things that couldn't have been</i>

370
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:32,280
<i>Seen if it weren't for these eyes</i>

371
00:23:32,280 --> 00:23:37,040
<i>Why? They begin to overflow</i>

372
00:23:37,040 --> 00:23:43,130
<i>So, if I were to be born again</i>

373
00:23:43,130 --> 00:23:48,960
<i>I would surely choose this place once more</i>

374
00:23:48,960 --> 00:23:54,970
<i>So, if we were to meet again</i>

375
00:23:54,970 --> 00:24:00,730
<i>I'd never let you go, I'd choose the present</i>

376
00:24:00,730 --> 00:24:03,690
<i>Even if no promises were made</i>

377
00:24:03,690 --> 00:24:06,610
<i>Even if I'm lost in days of loneliness</i>

378
00:24:06,610 --> 00:24:12,780
<i>Those tears will be alright,
dawn will surely break</i>

379
00:24:12,780 --> 00:24:15,450
<i>I'm whispering our lullaby</i>

380
00:24:15,450 --> 00:24:19,370
<i>for you to come back home</i>

381
00:24:20,180 --> 00:24:22,420
What do you mean by understanding relationships?

382
00:24:20,680 --> 00:24:23,150
You just seem like someone accustomed
to speaking with women. I don't like it.

383
00:24:20,970 --> 00:24:23,050
I'm pretty sure that would kill me.

384
00:24:22,410 --> 00:24:24,130
Let's go shopping together later.

385
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:24,600
We help each other when we're in need.

386
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:26,690
It happens naturally as people age.

387
00:24:25,010 --> 00:24:26,220
We're alive.

388
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:27,790
Do you really hate me that much?

389
00:24:27,790 --> 00:24:30,110
Those arguments are the
privilege of the young.
